# DTF tier manifest: terraform-origin-registry  (artifact-keeper#4356, PR #4357)
# Profile-set: filesystem + client.terraform (caddy TLS terminator aliased as
# tf.dtf.local in front of the backend, and the real hashicorp/terraform CLI).
#
# THE FEATURE (#4356, merged as #4357 / cae32abe, milestone 1.12.0)
# A hosted Terraform repository could not act as an OpenTofu/Terraform ORIGIN
# provider registry: the package document had no shasums_url /
# shasums_signature_url and an empty gpg_public_keys, and discovery was only
# served per repository, so `tofu init` / `terraform providers lock` against
# <host>/<ns>/<type> failed. The fix adds, for hosted repos:
#   GET /terraform/<repo>/v1/providers/<ns>/<type>/<ver>/SHA256SUMS
#       deterministic, "<sha256>  terraform-provider-<type>_<ver>_<os>_<arch>.zip"
#       per platform, sorted by filename, computed from stored artifacts
#   GET .../SHA256SUMS.sig
#       binary detached OpenPGP signature made with the repository's active
#       gpg signing key (cached 5 min per key + digest)
#   package document: shasums_url, shasums_signature_url,
#       signing_keys.gpg_public_keys[{key_id, ascii_armor}]
#   no key configured: both routes 404 "No signing key configured ..." and
#       the document keeps the legacy unsigned shape (fail closed)
#   GET /.well-known/terraform.json at the host root, answered from the repo
#       named by TERRAFORM_DEFAULT_REPO (read once at boot); unset, missing or
#       non-Terraform -> one generic 404
# The maintainer commit adds single-use, path-bound `?ticket=` download
# tickets (10 min TTL) on download_url, shasums_url and shasums_signature_url
# for an AUTHENTICATED caller, so Terraform's credential-less follow-up
# fetches work against a private repo; anonymous callers get plain paths.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   The oracle creates the repositories first, asserts the host route is 404
#   with the env unset, then recreates ONLY the backend on the same compose
#   project with TERRAFORM_DEFAULT_REPO=<public repo> through a tier-local
#   override (the qcmj-webhook-authz pattern; the DB volume survives), and at
#   the end once more with the key of a GENERIC repo.
#   Signature checks import the served ascii_armor into a throwaway GNUPGHOME
#   and require gpg's VALIDSIG fingerprint to equal the repo key's.
#   The real-client case trusts caddy's internal CA in the terraform container
#   and runs `terraform providers lock -platform=linux_amd64
#   -platform=darwin_arm64` with NO provider_installation block, so the CLI
#   uses host discovery (https://tf.dtf.local/.well-known/terraform.json), the
#   package documents, SHA256SUMS and the .sig, exactly as against a public
#   registry. The provider zips are inert fixtures (fixtures/terraform/build.sh)
#   and are never executed; `providers lock` only downloads and verifies.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)     host discovery 200 naming /terraform/<repo>/v1/providers/; signed
#             package document; SHA256SUMS exact and byte-stable; .sig verifies
#             (tamper does not); no-key routes 404 naming the missing key;
#             private-repo tickets on all three URLs, each good once without
#             credentials and refused on reuse, not usable on another path;
#             real terraform reports "signed, key ID <key>" and pins both zh:
#             hashes. RED on 1.11.3 (routes absent, discovery 404).
#   (CONTROL) both images: module upload / versions / X-Terraform-Get /
#             archive bytes and per-repo discovery; provider versions list and
#             the package document's core fields with download_url streaming
#             the zip; a no-key document keeps the legacy unsigned shape; host
#             discovery serves no document with the env unset (404; 1.11.3
#             has no route and answers 401) and the same response for a
#             non-Terraform default repo; a private repo refuses anonymous
#             callers on the document and the plain paths.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~60 calls back to back through one admin.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem client.terraform"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
